prayerTemplate:
PRAYER

In the light of the facts and circumstances stated above, the Plaintiff most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:

a) Pass a decree of specific performance of the agreement / contract dated {contract_date} directing the Defendant to execute and register a sale deed / lease / instrument of transfer in favour of the Plaintiff in respect of the suit property described in the Schedule, against payment of the balance consideration of Rs. {balance_consideration}/-, which the Plaintiff is ready and willing to pay;

b) In the event the Defendant fails to execute the sale deed within the time fixed, direct that the same be executed through the process of this Hon'ble Court under Order XXI Rule 34 CPC;

c) Direct the Defendant to deliver vacant and peaceful possession of the suit property to the Plaintiff;

d) In the alternative, and only if specific performance cannot be granted, award the Plaintiff damages of Rs. {damages_amount}/- under Section 21 of the Specific Relief Act, 1963, along with refund of earnest money of Rs. {earnest_money_paid}/-;

e) Award costs of the suit in favour of the Plaintiff;

f) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.

And for this act of kindness, the Plaintiff shall ever pray.
